  "id": "Compound::DB00703 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Methazolamide exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c19 and Cyp3a4, which are both involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. This binding leads to the participation of these enzymes in the conversion of arachidonic acid to epoxyeicosatrienoic acids, a process that is ultimately linked to Cyp2d6. The shared involvement of Cyp2c19 and Cyp3a4 in the same metabolic pathway suggests a potential mechanistic overlap, where Methazolamide may influence the activity of Cyp2d6 through the modulation of these upstream enzymes. The evidence from the three paths, with similar scores, supports a consistent pathway where Methazolamide's interaction with Cyp2c19 and Cyp3a4 contributes to the participation of Cyp2d6 in arachidonic acid metabolism. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Cyp2d6 in the enzymatic conversion of arachidonic acid, potentially under the influence of Methazolamide through a shared metabolic route.",
